NEW drumming  classes start next week people! New rhythm, new people and this has to be the best time of year to birth something new. So, why not sign yourself up for a 5 week African drumming course.  Our classes are fun, relaxed and full of valuable information that can get you playing a djembe the way a djembe is played! Most importantly spring has sprung and it it is time to have some fun.  Our classes teach traditional African djembe and dundun rhythms with a history of story and song to each rhythm.  These classes are structured with plenty of room to find your own rhythm and we love sharing and spreading technique that will help you feel confident playing djembe, so each week you will receive a Youtube video that recaps what  we covered in class.  What have you got to lose!? Come and try! All beginners and experienced, ages 8+ to adults welcome. Class details below: [Palmwoods Memorial Hall](/drumming-classes-sunshine-coast/palmwoods/) 6-7pm Tuesday evenings [Noosa](/drumming-classes-sunshine-coast/drumming-lessons-noosa/) @ The J 6-7pm Monday evenings [Maroochydore @ The Solbar](/drumming-classes-sunshine-coast/african-drumming-classes-at-solbar/) 5-6pm Wednesday evenings
